<gpx version="1.1" creator="Dartmoor traverse planner" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Dartmoor traverse — Ivybridge to Okehampton</name><desc>37.7 miles, +1395 m. Routed on the mapped path network where one exists (83% of the distance); the remainder crosses open moor with no path, marked by OPEN MOOR waypoints. Not a waymarked trail — carry OS Explorer OL28 and a compass. Camping is lawful on the Dartmoor commons within the National Park Authority&#x27;s published zones (Dartmoor Commons Act 1985 s.10(1); Darwall v DNPA [2025] UKSC 20). Two nights max, groups of six max, no fires, 100 m from any road.</desc></metadata>
